  "notes": "A short, high-frequency list of verbs takes a DATIVE where English expects a direct object: noceō, parcō, serviō, crēdō, ignōscō, imperō, persuādeō, placeō, studeō. Many verbs compounded with a preposition do the same. In the passive these verbs go impersonal: mihi persuādētur, 'I am persuaded'.",
